# Task 65.9.1D - Docker build-context hygiene for the `./frontend` build
# context. This context is used by `Dockerfile` (dev) and `Dockerfile.prod`
# (see `docker-compose.yml` / `docker-compose.prod.yml`
# `build.context: ./frontend` and `.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml`).
# Both Dockerfiles only ever `COPY react-export/...` - the actual Vite/React
# app that ships - never anything from the rest of this directory (a
# leftover Next.js scaffold: app/, components/, hooks/, lib/, styles/,
# types/, middleware.ts, next.config.mjs, tests/, etc. are real
# git-tracked source files, not touched here, since this task is
# build-context hygiene only and rule 7 of this task explicitly forbids
# guessing a blanket app/-style exclusion; that leftover scaffold is a
# separate cleanup question, not part of this task).
#
# Confirmed defect this file fixes (Task 65.9.1D): the previous bare
# `node_modules/` rule only matched the top-level scaffold's
# node_modules/, NOT `react-export/node_modules/` (Docker's .dockerignore
# matches bare/no-slash patterns only at the context root, unlike
# .gitignore - verified with an isolated `docker build` reproduction). As a
# result, every frontend image build shipped the *host's* Windows-built
# `react-export/node_modules/` (113MB, containing win32-x64 native
# `@esbuild`/`@rollup` binaries) into the final image via the Dockerfile's
# `COPY react-export/ ./` step, on top of the image's own correctly
# `npm install`-ed linux-x64 node_modules. `**/node_modules/` below matches
# at any depth and removes this.

# --- Git and editor metadata ---
.git
.idea/
.vscode/
.fleet/
.history/

# --- Secrets and local configuration ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Node caches and build output (recursive: covers both the top-level
#     scaffold's copies AND react-export/'s copies) ---
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/.turbo/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
**/.cache/

# --- Runtime data and logs ---
**/*.log
*.pid

# --- Tests: intentionally retained, not excluded here as a blanket rule.
#     `tests/` (bare/rooted) only matches the top-level scaffold's unused
#     Playwright/E2E directory - react-export's real unit tests are
#     colocated `*.test.ts(x)` files under `react-export/src/**`, which
#     this pattern cannot match and which remain fully available to both
#     the dev bind mount and any future in-container test run. ---
tests/

# --- OS temporary files ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
